{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>You shall not oppress.</b> This is one who withholds the wage of a hired worker (Bava Metzia 111a)." "<b>It shall not remain.</b> Feminine form — referring to the wage." "<b>Until the morning.</b> Scripture speaks of a day laborer — whose departure is from when the sun sets; therefore the time for collecting his wage is all the night. And in another place it says ״וְלֹא תָבוֹא עָלָיו הַשֶּׁמֶשׁ״ (Deuteronomy 24) — speaking of a night worker, whose completion of his wage is from when the column of dawn rises; therefore the time for collecting his wage is all the day, because the Torah gave the employer time, a season, to seek the coins (Bava Metzia 110a)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:07:08.820204100Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}